// v1.5.3 (#17): an integer assigned to an f64 from a VARIABLE.
//
// The declaration check compares the annotation against the RHS's SSA class, and
// a value read from a variable arrives as the uniform "ptr" - so this passed every
// check and stored the integer's BITS into the double. `set n: i64 = 5; fixed f:
// f64 = n;` printed 2.47033e-323.
//
// The same assignment from a literal or a call was already caught cleanly, which
// is why only the variable form got through. When the RHS is a bare variable its
// declared type is known, and that is what the check now uses.

df main() -> void {
    set n: i64 = 5;
    fixed f: f64 = n;
    echo!(f);
}
